    Node machine: keep the logical operators' paths out of the others' sweeps (#2524)
    
    On the 9700X the logical operators' rules, inlined into T's and C's
    dispatch, made clang leave node_machine_evaluate out of line, a call for
    every evaluated operand (227 of C's 3,024 samples on sqlite3.c). It is
    always inlined now, and the logical operators' rule, classification and
    label numbering, which few records reach, are out of line.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
    Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01EgbxndyALLrpzkYA1RTDzP
    Signed-off-by: David Gonzalez Martin <davidgmbb@gmail.com>

